Store the size of a ``NamedBlobFile`` and the dimensions of a ``NamedBlobImage`` when the data is written.
``getSize()`` and ``getImageSize()`` no longer read the whole blob, which on remote blob storages means downloading it, and ``getImageSize()`` no longer writes to the database.
Opening a ``NamedBlobFile`` for writing now also drops a persisted size.
Existing images with unknown dimensions ``(-1, -1)`` are no longer fixed when they are read, use ``backfill_metadata()`` for that.
[jensens]
